      "writtenOn": "2021-10-08T16:16:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Are there TCPC devices that are completely different from what is said in TCPCI specification?\n\nUnfortunately, yes. These days, those mostly take the form of TCPCs that are embedded logic blocks in the EC chip. (I believe stm32gx is an example of this.) They don\u0027t use I2C, which by itself would make them technically not TCPCI. More annoyingly, they sometimes have completely different register sets.\n\nps8xxx.c is TCPCI-compatible. I don\u0027t think you need to worry about non-TCPCI TCPCs for herobrine coverage. But I\u0027d suggest using \"TCPCI\" in the names and  descriptions of various things for this emulator, so it\u0027s not confusing later when somebody writes an emulator for the stm32gx.",
      "parentUuid": "fde16486_45d8af7a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 7,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 7,
        "endChar": 20
      },
