      "writtenOn": "2021-10-08T13:32:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Will be casting to uint16_t* endianness safe? I decided to use bit shifts to be sure that low byte will go to address reg and high byte goes to reg + 1. This makes easier handling I2C messages where low byte goes first.",
      "parentUuid": "a165f6ea_41cb0b8c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 124,
        "startChar": 0,
