      "lineNbr": 223,
      "author": {
        "id": 1511343
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-10-08T13:32:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I tried to emulate that TCPC has two 30 bytes buffers for incoming messages. First buffer is extended to 264 bytes when dev_cap2.LongMessage bit is set.",
      "parentUuid": "f63d3bc3_40f00991",
      "revId": "ea18505f2aed306413cc7509c44276d506a9b22b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2e77c53e_fc91d43e",
        "filename": "zephyr/emul/emul_tcpc.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 223,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-10-08T16:16:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe I\u0027m misunderstanding. If there might be a problem here, feel free to not fix it in this CL, because I don\u0027t think any of our real TCPCs actually support long message.\n\nThat being said, if what you\u0027re trying to do here is emulate receiving a long message, I would think you would want to pass in a single 264-byte buffer, not a linked list of 30-byte buffers. If the TCPC doesn\u0027t support long messages, then you would only read 31 bytes from that buffer. From the point of view of the EC, a long message should show up as one big message.\n\nThere is a PD feature where long message can be split into multiple short messages (\"chunking\") for TCPCs that don\u0027t support long messages. When this happens, it\u0027s transparent to the TCPC, which will only see a succession of short messages. You won\u0027t need to do anything specific in the emulator to support this.",
      "parentUuid": "17d4ab6b_b0d2b67f",
      "revId": "ea18505f2aed306413cc7509c44276d506a9b22b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
